  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "RC1_TEMPLATE_AND_EOS_MISMATCH",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "file": "scripts/colab/g4_jobs/job_qwen3_v3_vertibench_v2.py",
      "lines": "217-263, 489-493, 673-674",
      "explanation": "SFT supervises canonical_dsl with row-specific AGL/SPD/ETA plus trailing <|im_end|> (line 674), whereas build_language_matched_candidate_branches (lines 217-263) hardcodes static AGL=45,95;SPD=18 for DIVERT_SLZ, AGL=35,80;SPD=12 for ABORT_RETURN, and DUR=30;AGL=60 for HOLD_LOITER, and _score_live_branch_logprobs (line 490) omits <|im_end|>. Teacher-forcing mismatched hardcoded tokens heavily penalizes even the true gold branch, driving CV NLL up to 1.9915 nats (vs ln(14)=2.639 uniform)."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC2_BOILERPLATE_DILUTION_AT_GAMMA_1",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "file": "scripts/colab/g4_jobs/job_qwen3_v3_vertibench_v2.py",
      "lines": "355-364, 513-514; ml/copilot/calibrate_conformal.py:346-359",
      "explanation": "All 14 candidate branches share 70-85% deterministic boilerplate DSL tokens whose log-probs are ~0 after SFT (sft_mean_loss=0.08438). Dividing sum_logprob by n_tok^gamma at gamma=1.0 dilutes the 1-3 discriminative decision tokens by ~25-32x and introduces length bias between short HOLD_LOITER and longer DIVERT/CLARIFY strings, flattening softmax posteriors (forcing tau*=0.318 yet leaving ECE=0.1744-0.2950)."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC3_NAIVE_LAC_NONCONFORMITY_TAIL_COLLAPSE",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "file": "scripts/colab/g4_jobs/job_qwen3_v3_vertibench_v2.py",
      "lines": "371-378; ml/copilot/calibrate_conformal.py:425-527",
      "explanation": "_run_mondrian_audit uses naive LAC/THR nonconformity s_i = 1 - p(y_i*). Because the ADVERSARIAL bucket (25% of cal/test) has 44.93% AST accuracy, >5% of calibration rows fall in a low-p(y*) error tail, pushing q_hat to 0.9479-0.9774 and setting a static probability floor p_min = 0.0226-0.0521. With 14 compressed branches, 6.6-8.4 candidates exceed p_min on every sample -> 0.0% singleton_exec_pct. Crucially, fixing RC1+RC2 so gold ranks in top-2/top-3 is also required for RAPS/APS to yield singletons."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC4_SHARED_CAL_SPLIT_AND_SINGLE_SCALAR_TAU",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "file": "scripts/colab/g4_jobs/job_qwen3_v3_vertibench_v2.py",
      "lines": "355-378",
      "explanation": "A single scalar tau*=0.318372 is fit on all 2,000 cal rows and reused across all language and SNR strata before fitting group q_hat on the exact same 2,000 rows, ignoring per-stratum ECE divergence (S1_Cruise=0.1622 vs S2_Hover=0.2508 vs MIX=0.2950) and weakening strict split exchangeability."
    }
  ],
